tf-qwen35-cuda nll: one engine's teacher-forced logprobs, for comparing a checkpoint's quality across engines.

The kl mode compares bf16 and fp8 caches with two engines, which a 70 GiB checkpoint cannot hold twice on one GB10.
`tf-qwen35-cuda <model> nll <ids file> <out.json> <skip> [fp8]` runs ids[0..skip] as prompt chunks and the rest
through verify windows (the path replies take), and writes each window row's logprob of the next id (float64 log
softmax of its bf16 logits) as a JSON array, printing the mean NLL. bench/nll.py compares it with SGLang's
input_token_logprobs on the same ids. Test tool only: the server is unchanged.

